    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
      {
        "@value": "CPTG is used to record the general information about static cone penetration tests.\nPressuremeter tests using CPT equipment (e.g. cone or driven pressuremeter) shall be recorded in the PMTG and associated groups.\nCPTG_FILT and CPTG_FRIC are included as they are reporting requirements of BS1377 and BS EN ISO 22476-1.\nCPTG_WATA is required to clarify origin of water level recorded in CPTG_WAT.\nCPTG_REM is used to transfer comments on the test and any interpreted parameters. CPTG_REM may refer to the STND group where full information on standards and references could be provided.\nCPT testing is frequently carried out by specialist sub-contractors. CPTG_CONT is included to record name of specialist sub-contractor.\nCPTG_CAR and CPTG_SLAR are included to transfer information used to calculate qt and ft.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
